// Slides (if-slides-api): render a slide deck from a structured description and fetch it again
// by its ID. One of the record types of the hub (dec-records-per-type).
//
// The hub keeps the input of every deck (title, slides, author, time) and the rendered output in
// its archive (dec-yaml-git-storage), so decks survive a restart. Rendering is deterministic
// (con-no-intelligence): the same title and slides give the same bytes.
//
// A deck has an ID such as "slides/42". The stage shows a deck by this ID (artifact.shown in
// session.proto): "artifact" is the general word for anything the stage can show, and the part
// before the slash names its type.
//
// Every call needs an access token of a participant (see identity.proto). A stage link cannot
// use this interface: the stage loads decks inside the hub. A sentence that is off the record
// must not go into a deck (dec-off-the-record).

